{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at the end</b> מקץ is said here and מקץ is said of Abraham: מקץ עשר שנים (at the end of ten years). Just as there it is ten, so too here, at the end of ten years. And the meaning of ויהי מקץ, that is, at the end of ten plus two years:" "<b>ויהי מקץ שנתים ימים ופרעה חלם</b> in gematria: עשר שנים (ten years):"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The verse at the end of which 'מקץ עשר שנים' is said of Abraham is not cited; it refers to the reckoning in the Sages' tradition that from Joseph's being sold until his ascent to power was twenty-two years, ten of which had already elapsed before the two years of this verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:07.990665988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}